<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n115250" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ψ ψ,</span></b> 
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψεῖ</span></b>  (q. v.), τό, indecl., twenty-third letter of the Ionic
		alphabet, <i><span class="en">
			Pl.
			<u>Cra.</u>
			427a
		</span></i>, Callias ap.<i><span class="en">
			Ath.
			10.453d
		</span></i>: not used in the Attic alphabet: in the Western Gr. alphabets it
		represents the sound <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ</span> (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>kh</i>): with the value
			<i>ps</i> it is found in <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				1
			</span></i> (Nubia, <span class="entity">vi B. C.</span>), etc.: as a numberal,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψ́</span>
			=
			<i><span class="en">
				700
			</span></i>, but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">
				y'
			</span>
			=
			<i><span class="en">
				700
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				000
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
